From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:01:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] client: expose ordered observations and joined shutdown

Install a synchronous observer before workers start, report each received query-set transition and connection state, and report terminal closure without turning snapshots into a database change log. Keep the existing bounded state channel best effort so a full receiver cannot block reconnects or shutdown.

Give cloned clients one cancellation-safe joined close operation covering both background tasks, retain final-drop cancellation, and preserve buffered stream and submitted-mutation semantics. Add local WebSocket lifecycle fixtures and document the replay, observation and distribution boundaries.
